       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Dose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 6 mg rapid IV bolus over 1–2 s, given as close to the pt as poss and followed by a rapid saline flush; if the SVT persists after 1–2 min, give 12 mg rapid IV bolus, which may be repeated once. Doses above 12 mg are ⍉recommended."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "SE:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a brief (2–3 s) ♡ standstill can occur; transient or prolonged asystole, sometimes fatal, has been reported. It can cause short-lasting first-, second- or third-degree AV block; give ⍉further doses after high-level block. Asthma has worsened after IV adenosine."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " second- or third-degree AV block, or sinus node dz (sick sinus syndrome, Sxtomatic brady), unless a functioning pacemaker = in place. ⍉in bronchospasm (ex, asthma)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " methylxanthines (caffeine, theophylline) antagonize it, so lrger doses may be needed or it may ⍉work; dipyridamole potentiates it, so smaller doses may work. Carbamazepine can deepen the ♡ block. Use w caution w digoxin (± verapamil): rare VF has been reported."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
